title Run after the kick
intro Blue is about to pass into the space behind Red.
flip vertical

setup
  lineup 7v7
  player R-CB at 78, 40
  player R-RB at 74, 20
  player R-LB at 74, 56
  player B-LF at 74, 30
  player B-CM at 55, 34
  ball with B-CM

step
  caption Watch where Blue is when the ball is played. The yellow line marks the last defender.
  draw line 78, 0 to 78, 68

step
  caption Blue kicks it into the space behind the defender. Their striker is still behind the line — they can sprint past after the kick.
  ball to 84, 30
  arrow from B-CM to ball
  draw line 78, 0 to 78, 68
  duration 1200

question
  prompt Is the Blue striker offside?
  answer No
  wrong Yes
  wrong Yes, they are past the defender
  wrong Only if they score
  correct Not offside.
  why Blue was behind the defender at the moment of the kick. Running past afterwards is a great move, not a foul.

question
  prompt When does the ref check where you are standing?
  answer When the ball is kicked
  wrong When you get the ball
  wrong When you shoot
  wrong At the end of the play
  correct When the ball is kicked.
  why Offside is judged the second the ball leaves your teammate's foot, not when it reaches you.
